direction: down

title: |md
  ## bpf_dynptr: dynamic-size writes to ringbuf
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

problem: "Problem with reserve():\n\nbpf_ringbuf_reserve(rb, sz, 0)\nrequires sz to be constant at\nBPF compile time.\n\nWhat if you don't know the size yet?\n(e.g., variable-length string,\npacket payload of unknown length)\n\nOld solutions:\n- Reserve max size, waste tail bytes\n- Use bpf_ringbuf_output (always copies)\n- Keep size capped at small max" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
}

solution: "Solution: bpf_ringbuf_reserve_dynptr\n\nstruct bpf_dynptr ptr;\nbpf_ringbuf_reserve_dynptr(&rb, sz, 0, &ptr);\n\n/* dynamically write to the dynptr: */\nbpf_dynptr_write(&ptr, 0,\n    &header, sizeof(header));\nbpf_dynptr_write(&ptr, sizeof(header),\n    payload, payload_len);\n\nbpf_ringbuf_submit_dynptr(&ptr, 0);\n\n✅ Variable size at runtime\n✅ Verifier tracks bounds via dynptr type\n✅ Same throughput as direct reserve" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
}

verifier: "Verifier tracking\n\nThe Verifier tracks bpf_dynptr as a\nspecial pointer type with bounds.\n\n- bpf_dynptr_write(p, off, src, len)\n  checks off + len ≤ p.size\n- same for bpf_dynptr_read\n\nCaller can't OOB-write even if\noff/len come from packet data." {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
}

problem -> solution
solution -> verifier
